From eb38f440b346e7b81b7dc80bd56e90916807caed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Mar 2026 23:12:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] Add safe lmkd defaults, heap floor, and PSI strategy for GSI
 builds

Disable critical_upgrade and enable kill_heaviest_task for more
predictable memory management across diverse hardware.

Set a minimum dalvik.vm.heapgrowthlimit of 256m. Some vendor
build.prop files ship an aggressive 16m limit tuned for their stock ROM.
Android 16's system_server requires significantly more than 16m to
initialise; without this override rw-system.sh crashes early (empty vndk
var arithmetic) and the vendor value is never corrected, causing
system_server to OOM-loop and the device to be stuck on bootsplash.

Force PSI-based kill strategy on all devices. Vendors with older
Android 12 bases set ro.lmk.use_minfree_levels=true which selects the
legacy kill strategy requiring cgroup v1. On cgroup v2 (standard since
Android 12), lmkd exits immediately with 'Old kill strategy can only be
used with v1 cgroup hierarchy'. Without lmkd, ActivityManager cannot
manage process lifecycle, causing cascading ANRs, SystemUI failure, and
boot timeouts exceeding 90 seconds.

Setting ro.lmk.use_new_strategy=true in system.prop forces PSI-based
monitoring regardless of vendor minfree_levels setting. This takes
effect before lmkd starts, unlike the rw-system.sh ro.config.low_ram
workaround which runs too late.
---
 system.prop | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/system.prop b/system.prop
index f3c0c45..1b4e40a 100644
--- a/system.prop
+++ b/system.prop
@@ -49,3 +49,21 @@ bluetooth.profile.sap.server.enabled?=true
 
 # Samsung vendors default to a Samsung-specific gadget for MTP. Set this to use AOSP's functionfs MTP
 vendor.usb.use_ffs_mtp=1
+
+# lmkd tuning: safe defaults for GSI across diverse hardware
+# Disable critical_upgrade to prevent overly aggressive kills on devices
+# where memory pressure detection may not work correctly (e.g., older kernels)
+ro.lmk.critical_upgrade=false
+# Kill heaviest task first for more predictable memory management
+ro.lmk.kill_heaviest_task=true
+
+# Heap floor: vendor build.prop values as low as 16m are seen in the wild.
+# Android 16 system_server needs ~200m+ to initialise; override with a safe
+# minimum while preserving larger vendor values via the ? default operator.
+dalvik.vm.heapgrowthlimit?=256m
+dalvik.vm.heapsize?=512m
+# Force PSI-based kill strategy on all devices. Vendors with older kernels
+# may set ro.lmk.use_minfree_levels=true which selects the legacy cgroup v1
+# kill strategy. On cgroup v2 (standard since Android 12), this causes lmkd
+# to exit immediately, breaking process lifecycle management entirely.
+ro.lmk.use_new_strategy=true
